diff --git a/findings/help/runner_start.txt b/findings/help/runner_start.txt
index f9d3ed4..49f89b4 100644
--- a/findings/help/runner_start.txt
+++ b/findings/help/runner_start.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,17 @@
-OVERVIEW: Start the runner with WDA and keep it alive for interactive use.
+OVERVIEW: Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android) and keep it alive
+for interactive use.
+
+Without --detach the command stays in the foreground, streams the runner's
+output to stderr and holds the session until Ctrl-C (or `grantiva runner stop`
+from another shell); it then stops the runner, removes the session files and
+releases the device. Interrupted, it exits 130. With --detach it returns once
+the driver is up and the runner keeps the session until `grantiva runner stop`.
+
+--json prints one document: {"status": "started" | "already_running", "pid":
+<number>, "port": <number>, "platform": "ios" | "android", plus "bundleId" and
+"udid" on iOS or "applicationId" and "serial" on Android, and "log" with
+--detach}. "bundle_id" (and "udid" on Android) are kept for compatibility and
+are deprecated.
 
 USAGE: grantiva runner start [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--platform <platform>] [--bundle-id <bundle-id>] [--simulator <simulator>] [--application-id <application-id>] [--emulator <emulator>] [--device <device>] [--headless] [--detach]
 
diff --git a/findings/help/runner_stop.txt b/findings/help/runner_stop.txt
index 0c3ef62..f75f561 100644
--- a/findings/help/runner_stop.txt
+++ b/findings/help/runner_stop.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,16 @@
 OVERVIEW: Stop the running runner session.
 
+Stops the session `grantiva runner start` recorded in .grantiva/session.json:
+the runner gets SIGINT, then SIGTERM and SIGKILL if it does not exit, and its
+session files and device lease are removed. Without one, it releases a
+`grantiva run --keep-alive` session started from this directory (every one, if
+there are several) the way Ctrl-C would, by sending that grantiva process
+SIGINT, and waits for it to exit. A run whose flows had already finished keeps
+the ready file it wrote (`passed` or `failed`): the ready file is written once,
+and the `stopped` result here is the record of the release. Sessions started
+from other directories are left alone. With no session at all it prints "No
+active session found." and exits 0.
+
 USAGE: grantiva runner stop [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]
 
 OPTIONS:
